  "summary": "Postinstall beacon exfiltrates host identifiers to hardcoded external endpoint",
  "details": "On `npm install`, the package's postinstall lifecycle script collects installer host identifiers (hostname, platform, architecture, Node.js version, package name, npm lifecycle event) and POSTs them as JSON to the hardcoded remote endpoint https://bhvte4h4.instances.poc.jchunt.top/wct-st. The beacon fires automatically with no consent, configuration, or opt-out. The package name resembles the deprecated `web-component-tester`, consistent with a typosquat / dependency-confusion beacon shape.",
